  "title": "Cucumber and feta salad",
  "description": "Feta cheese is naturally salty so be mindful to avoid adding too much salt.",
  "editorial": {
    "content": "This cucumber, feta, and mint salad is not only tasty but also very refreshing. It is an ideal summer meal. This salad goes very well with pita bread. <!--WPRM Recipe 21552-->\n<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe\">\n\t<h2 class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-name\">Cucumber and feta salad</h2>\n\t<img class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-image\" src=\"https://mycafegourmand.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/08/IMG_2143.Blog_-150x150.png\"/>\t<p class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-summary\">\n\t\tFeta cheese is naturally salty so be mindful to avoid adding too much salt.\t</p>\n\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-equipment\">\n\t\t\t</div>\n\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-ingredients\">\n\t\t<ul><li>1 long cucumber (diced)</li><li>200 g feta cheese (diced)</li><li>1/4 bunch Fresh mint (chopped)</li><li>Salt and freshly ground black pepper</li><li>Some freshly squeezed lemon juice ((optional))</li><li>Some olive oil</li></ul>\t</div>\n\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-instructions\">\n\t\t<ol><li>In a medium bowl, combine cucumber, feta, and fresh mint. Season with salt and pepper. Drizzle with lemon juice and olive oil. Toss gently. Cover and let stand in the fridge for at least a half hour.</li></ol>\t</div>\n\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-notes\">\n\t\t\t</div>\n\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-meta\">\n\t\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-meta-course\">Salads</div>\t</div>\n</div>\n<!--End WPRM Recipe-->",
    "excerpt": null
  },
